199
00:25:03,438 --> 00:25:11,888
We have large customers that have migrated the Exadata workloads onto LOITB and have invested heavily and standardized on LOITB.

200
00:25:12,078 --> 00:25:15,268
So these are just four engines out of the 15 or so that we have.

201
00:25:27,118 --> 00:25:32,100
Now, earlier this year, we talked about the million agent world and it's arriving much faster than expected.

202
00:25:32,366 --> 00:25:39,808
We're moving from single co-pilot kind of transactions to networks of agents that are collaborating and working simultaneously.

203
00:25:40,046 --> 00:25:49,728
And when they reason and they work all at once, sudden traffic spikes can overwhelm your core databases and it can compete with your business applications for resources.

204
00:25:49,888 --> 00:25:56,036
Traditional operational databases simply cannot scale to the dynamic agent workloads.

205
00:25:56,526 --> 00:26:00,164
Agents require massive scale in unpredictable bursts.

206
00:26:00,462 --> 00:26:07,012
Traditional database replicas also do not scale to this, and they hit the hard architecture limit very soon.

207
00:26:08,334 --> 00:26:11,524
To solve this, we launched Postgres for Agents just last month.

208
00:26:11,918 --> 00:26:25,572
With traditional database architectures, we're designed for human applications, while newer architectures that have evolved relied on caching layers that live above the object storage, which creates scaling and cost challenges.

209
00:26:26,048 --> 00:26:28,356
We took a completely different approach.

210
00:26:28,718 --> 00:26:34,820
Postgres for agents in AlloyDB introduces a new agentic database architecture.

211
00:26:35,854 --> 00:26:40,868
This architecture bridges the gap with purpose-built architecture for agentic workloads.

212
00:26:41,168 --> 00:26:48,452
It enables enterprises to scale agents without risking the core operations, which is extremely important.

213
00:26:49,006 --> 00:26:55,556
Lloydb rapidly scales Postgres reader nodes to 1000 plus with instant elasticity.

214
00:26:56,462 --> 00:27:06,468
These nodes react to the agent reasoning burst, then will dynamically scale down to zero when there is no work to be done just to optimize the cost.

215
00:27:07,008 --> 00:27:18,468
It provides unrivaled throughput, handles over 8 million IOPS, 3 million transactions per second, with up to the second operational data on production.

216
00:27:18,734 --> 00:27:24,068
But what is more important is that it does it without impacting your production database.

217
00:27:24,462 --> 00:27:32,528
Agent execution is 100% sandbox with total compute and I/O isolation from the primary line of business application.

218
00:27:32,846 --> 00:27:40,900
Finally, native integration with Gemini Agent Platform as well as Zero ETL Federation to BigQuery and Spark for Lakehouse Analytics is available.

