413
00:47:08,238 --> 00:47:10,788
This is the case where we don't have the context set up yet.

414
00:47:11,246 --> 00:47:18,628
And you can see that the user asked a question about uh, you know, show me active family homes around Austin in top-rated school districts.

415
00:47:19,248 --> 00:47:23,204
unfortunately, there just isn't enough context for the agent to know how to answer that question correctly.

416
00:47:24,654 --> 00:47:26,208
But let's see what we can do with query data.

417
00:47:26,542 --> 00:47:32,768
We can curate extra context with context engineering agent in quad Code, codex, or Antigravity.

418
00:47:33,038 --> 00:47:36,036
Context Engineering Agent closes this gap in three steps.

419
00:47:36,448 --> 00:47:39,236
One, it analyzes your application artifacts.

420
00:47:39,568 --> 00:47:43,488
Two, it helps curate a thorough data set for the anticipated queries.

421
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:46,688
Three, it automates the hill climbing to improve performance.

422
00:47:46,990 --> 00:47:50,288
The optimized context set is published to Knowledge Catalog.

423
00:47:50,638 --> 00:47:53,540
Real queries in production may deviate from our data set.

424
00:47:53,806 --> 00:48:02,688
Your application can log queries that are not covered by context, feed it back as an input to the context generation agent, and the agent will use this to help guide its optimization.

